      "message": "\u003e would be to just enable MAPPER_ENABLE_DEBUG by default for any build, \nnot just debug builds (and disabling it by default in the recipe).\n\nThis will not improve coverage of the production code path. We would be running static analysis on a debug build and then compiling something else for the full image, defeating the point of doing static analysis in the first place.\n\n\u003e Another thought is changing the name from DEBUG to PROFILE since that is what is actually going on here, and removing the linkage \nto debug builds.\n\nMade a new revision which has the class members for profiling present by default but still guards the code using those members.\n\nI believe this will introduce only minimal overhead (allocating a few extra bytes for storing the extra class members) while keeping the implementation simple without templated base class.\n\nLet me know if this new patchset works better 👍",
